# Retired pixel atlas. The daemon draws vector paths now and never loads these;
# `build_sheet.py` still bakes them from the ASCII grids in sprites.py if you
# want the old art back, but nothing at runtime or install time needs them.
sprites.png
sprites.json

# vector_paths.py and vector_prop_paths.py are generated too, by
# build_vector.py, but they are deliberately NOT ignored. They are small,
# deterministic text, and committing them means a fresh clone runs with no
# build step - which the binary atlas above could never offer. install.sh
# regenerates them anyway, so editing the SVGs still works.

# preview.png is NOT here on purpose: README.md embeds it, so it has to be
# committed or the image is a dead link on GitHub / a fresh clone.

# Runtime state - per-machine, recreated by notify.sh / guy.py
daemon.pid
state.json
prompt_ts
pos.json
prefs.json
guy.log
guy.crash.log

# Live session data, lives outside the repo by default but DECK_GUY_HOME can
# point it here during testing
.deck-guy/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
